      "message": "See https://buganizer.corp.google.com/issues/189705988#comment5 for some analysis.\nPasting it here.\n\nnet/sched/Kconfig:111:config NET_SCH_MULTIQ\nnet/sched/Kconfig-112-  tristate \"Hardware Multiqueue-aware Multi Band Queuing (MULTIQ)\"\nnet/sched/Kconfig-113-  help\nnet/sched/Kconfig-114-    Say Y here if you want to use an n-band queue packet scheduler\nnet/sched/Kconfig-115-    to support devices that have multiple hardware transmit queues.\nnet/sched/Kconfig-116-\nnet/sched/Kconfig-117-    To compile this code as a module, choose M here: the\nnet/sched/Kconfig-118-    module will be called sch_multiq.\n\n^ yes, definitely, not sure why it\u0027s off\n\nCONFIG_NET_SCH_NETEM\u003dy\n\n^ not sure why this isn\u0027t already enabled, it was technically required by R,\nI have a local change myself to enable it that I haven\u0027t yet sent up\n\n(and apparently it is only recommended...\nandroid-4.19/android-recommended.config:96:CONFIG_NET_SCH_NETEM\u003dy\nandroid-5.10/android-recommended.config:96:CONFIG_NET_SCH_NETEM\u003dy\nandroid-5.4/android-recommended.config:96:CONFIG_NET_SCH_NETEM\u003dy)\n\nnet/sched/Kconfig:556:config CLS_U32_MARK\nnet/sched/Kconfig-557-  bool \"Netfilter marks support\"\nnet/sched/Kconfig-558-  depends on NET_CLS_U32\nnet/sched/Kconfig-559-  help\nnet/sched/Kconfig-560-    Say Y here to be able to use netfilter marks as u32 key.\n\n^ reasonable enough, though dangerous if used in a way conflicting with mainline modules\n\nnet/sched/Kconfig:590:config NET_CLS_FLOW\nnet/sched/Kconfig-591-  tristate \"Flow classifier\"\nnet/sched/Kconfig-592-  select NET_CLS\nnet/sched/Kconfig-593-  help\nnet/sched/Kconfig-594-    If you say Y here, you will be able to classify packets based on\nnet/sched/Kconfig-595-    a configurable combination of packet keys. This is mostly useful\nnet/sched/Kconfig-596-    in combination with SFQ.\nnet/sched/Kconfig-597-\nnet/sched/Kconfig-598-    To compile this code as a module, choose M here: the\nnet/sched/Kconfig-599-    module will be called cls_flow.\n\n^ no complaints\n\nnet/sched/Kconfig:666:config NET_EMATCH_CMP\nnet/sched/Kconfig-667-  tristate \"Simple packet data comparison\"\nnet/sched/Kconfig-668-  depends on NET_EMATCH\nnet/sched/Kconfig-669-  help\nnet/sched/Kconfig-670-    Say Y here if you want to be able to classify packets based on\nnet/sched/Kconfig-671-    simple packet data comparisons for 8, 16, and 32bit values.\nnet/sched/Kconfig-672-\nnet/sched/Kconfig-673-    To compile this code as a module, choose M here: the\nnet/sched/Kconfig-674-    module will be called em_cmp.\n\n^ I guess this is either u32 or like u32 - again ok.\n\nnet/sched/Kconfig:676:config NET_EMATCH_NBYTE\nnet/sched/Kconfig-677-  tristate \"Multi byte comparison\"\nnet/sched/Kconfig-678-  depends on NET_EMATCH\nnet/sched/Kconfig-679-  help\nnet/sched/Kconfig-680-    Say Y here if you want to be able to classify packets based on\nnet/sched/Kconfig-681-    multiple byte comparisons mainly useful for IPv6 address comparisons.\nnet/sched/Kconfig-682-\nnet/sched/Kconfig-683-    To compile this code as a module, choose M here: the\nnet/sched/Kconfig-684-    module will be called em_nbyte.\n\n^ basically more u32 - again ok.\n\nnet/sched/Kconfig:696:config NET_EMATCH_META\nnet/sched/Kconfig-697-  tristate \"Metadata\"\nnet/sched/Kconfig-698-  depends on NET_EMATCH\nnet/sched/Kconfig-699-  help\nnet/sched/Kconfig-700-    Say Y here if you want to be able to classify packets based on\nnet/sched/Kconfig-701-    metadata such as load average, netfilter attributes, socket\nnet/sched/Kconfig-702-    attributes and routing decisions.\n\n^ uncertain of this one, but I guess ok.\n\nnet/sched/Kconfig:707:config NET_EMATCH_TEXT\nnet/sched/Kconfig-708-  tristate \"Textsearch\"\nnet/sched/Kconfig-709-  depends on NET_EMATCH\nnet/sched/Kconfig-710-  select TEXTSEARCH\nnet/sched/Kconfig-711-  select TEXTSEARCH_KMP\nnet/sched/Kconfig-712-  select TEXTSEARCH_BM\nnet/sched/Kconfig-713-  select TEXTSEARCH_FSM\nnet/sched/Kconfig-714-  help\nnet/sched/Kconfig-715-    Say Y here if you want to be able to classify packets based on\nnet/sched/Kconfig-716-    textsearch comparisons.\n\n^ seems like a bad idea, but I guess it\u0027s ok, we don\u0027t have to use it.\n\nnet/sched/Kconfig:857:config NET_ACT_SKBEDIT\nnet/sched/Kconfig-858-  tristate \"SKB Editing\"\nnet/sched/Kconfig-859-  depends on NET_CLS_ACT\nnet/sched/Kconfig-860-  help\nnet/sched/Kconfig-861-    Say Y here to change skb priority or queue_mapping settings.\n\n^ yes, fine.\n\n--\n\nSo in general I support enabling these things, though am worried that vendors/oems may build something conflicting with mainline code out of it.  Because we may end up using these things in the future, and technically we (mainline) already \u0027owns\u0027 the tc configuration of network devices.",
